# HORO-1296: the XcodeGen release that GlomerisMenuBar.xcodeproj is generated
# with, pinned so the drift guard is meaningful.
#
# Different XcodeGen versions emit different `project.pbxproj` bytes for the
# same `project.yml`. Without a pin, the guard would either report drift that
# isn't there (CI's version newer than the committer's) or, in the other
# direction, "fix" the committed project into whatever CI happens to install.
# Pinning makes "regenerate and diff" a statement about `project.yml`, not
# about the toolchain.
#
# Both `scripts/check-xcodeproj-matches-xcodegen.sh` and the `xcodeproj-drift`
# job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` read this file, so the version lives in
# exactly one place. To upgrade: bump both fields, regenerate, and commit the
# resulting `.xcodeproj` in the same commit.
#
# sha256 is of the `xcodegen.zip` asset on that release
# (https://github.com/yonaskolb/XcodeGen/releases). GitHub release assets can
# be replaced after publication, so the version tag alone is not a sufficient
# pin for something CI downloads and executes.
version=2.46.0
